GAL22V10
DECODE

AS   DS   RW   A19  A18  A17  A16  FC0  FC1  FC2  RESET GND
XDTACK OVL BERR DTACK DUART JSEL ROE RD   WR   ROMCE RAMCE VCC

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; MC68008 core board, GAL1: address decoding and boot overlay.
; galasm syntax: "/" = pin low, "*" = AND, "+" = OR.
;
;   $00000-$7FFFF  512K SRAM (AS6C4008)
;   $80000-$BFFFF  256K flash (SST39SF020A)
;   $C0000-$CFFFF  Junior bus window (bridge in GAL2), JSEL
;   $D0000-$EFFFF  spare -> BERR
;   $F0000-$FFFFF  68681 DUART (16 registers, mirrored), not during IACK
;
; Pin 1 is AS. It clocks the OVL register on its rising edge (end of each
; bus cycle) and is also used as a normal input.
;
; Boot overlay: AR (RESET low) clears the register, and because OVL is an
; active-low registered output its pin then reads HIGH = overlay on. While
; OVL is high, reads from $00000-$7FFFF come from the flash, so the CPU
; fetches SSP/PC from flash. The first bus cycle in $80000-$BFFFF drives
; OVL low at the end of that cycle; from then on RAM is at $00000.
; Writes always go to RAM. Verify on the bench: OVL must be high after
; reset (scope pin 14 with RESET held low).
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

AR      = /RESET

/OVL.R  = /OVL
        + A19 * /A18

; SRAM: whole lower half once the overlay is off; writes always.
/RAMCE  = /AS * /A19 * /OVL
        + /AS * /A19 * /RW

; Flash: its own range, plus reads of the lower half during the overlay.
/ROMCE  = /AS * A19 * /A18
        + /AS * /A19 * OVL * RW

; Shared strobes for SRAM and flash (/OE and /WE). Writes to the flash
; range reach the flash's /WE, so it can be reprogrammed in circuit with
; the SST unlock sequence.
/RD     = /DS * RW
/WR     = /DS * /RW

; Junior bus window. GAL2 runs the PHI2-synchronous cycle and its DTACK.
/JSEL   = /AS * A19 * A18 * /A17 * /A16

; Output enable of the 74HCT573 read latch (bus data -> CPU).
/ROE    = /AS * /DS * RW * A19 * A18 * /A17 * /A16

; 68681 chip select, qualified with DS so write data is valid.
; IACK cycles ($FFFFx with FC = 111) are excluded; GAL2 decodes those.
/DUART  = /AS * /DS * A19 * A18 * A17 * A16 * /FC0
        + /AS * /DS * A19 * A18 * A17 * A16 * /FC1
        + /AS * /DS * A19 * A18 * A17 * A16 * /FC2

; DTACK to the CPU. GAL1 always drives it: low with no wait states for
; SRAM and flash, and low when the external DTACK (XDTACK, pin 13) is low.
; XDTACK is a wired-OR line with a 4k7 pull-up, driven by GAL2's JDTACK
; (Junior window) and the 68681 DTACKN (registers and IACK vector).
/DTACK  = /AS * /A19
        + /AS * A19 * /A18
        + /AS * /XDTACK

; Bus error for the spare ranges $D0000-$EFFFF.
/BERR   = /AS * A19 * A18 * /A17 * A16
        + /AS * A19 * A18 * A17 * /A16

DESCRIPTION
68008 core board GAL1: SRAM $00000, flash $80000 with boot overlay,
Junior bus window $C0000 (JSEL), 68681 at $F0000, DTACK and BERR.
